FamilyRoots Platform ("Family Together") - Complete Project Overview & Architecture Guide
=======================================================================================
Platform: FamilyRoots ("Family Together")
Backend: NestJS 11 + Express + Prisma 7 ORM + PostgreSQL + Redis + Nodemailer + Stripe
Frontend: Next.js 16 + React 19 + TypeScript + TailwindCSS v4 + Redux Toolkit RTK Query

1. Executive Summary:
FamilyRoots is a privacy-first, multi-generational family tree and archival digital sanctuary.
Families can document ancestors, preserve multimedia memories, store legal records, coordinate
reunions, and manage kinship links under strict multi-tenant isolation.

2. Architecture Breakdown:
- Backend: REST APIs with Passport JWT auth, Swagger docs (/api/docs), multi-schema Prisma 7, Redis token cache.
- Frontend: Next.js 16 App Router, Kinship Modern design, interactive 2D canvas tree, RTK query caching.

3. Key Modules:
- Decoupled Person Model: Ancestors exist independently of user logins.
- Real-Time Deduplication: Search existing relatives and link them to prevent duplicate rows.
- Auto-Credential Generation: Adding living members with an email auto-creates accounts and sends welcome emails.
- Kinship Graph Engine: 18+ relationship types with bi-directional resolution.
- Media Vault: Photo/video stories with carousel sliders and lightbox modal.
- 100MB Document Vault: High-resolution scans with custom 100MB body parser.
- Events & Heatmap: RSVP tracking and GitHub-style green activity heatmap.
- Stripe Billing: Free, Premium, and Lifetime sanctuary subscriptions.

4. Roles & Dashboards:
- SUPER_ADMIN (/admin-dashboard/super): Database backups, node health, encryption keys.
- ADMIN (/admin-dashboard): Cross-tenant user administration, analytics, support.
- OWNER (/owner-dashboard): Sanctuary control, tree canvas, members, memories, events, billing.
- MEMBER/USER (/user-dashboard): Personal lineage, memory feed, RSVP, account credentials.
- VIEWER (/user-dashboard): Read-only guest access.

